// XFAIL: RT-446h: UNSOUND: (RT-446's mechanism, a projection) a field typed by an associated-type projection, `struct V<X: Tr> { o: X::O }` with `type O = &'static u64` for Y, takes a local's borrow: `V { o: &*b }` returned from mk with b a Box local is accepted, and main reads it after the free; rustc E0597 (`*b` does not live long enough) (0.30.2)
// From the review of g302static (its form g04_assoc_type_field). Since v0.30.1 at
// least, and on the release build with g302static merged (the same use
// after free under --check-alloc). RT-446's root through a projection: the
// field's type is `X::O`, which normalizes to `&'static u64` for X = Y,
// and the region walk does not see the 'static in it.
// FLAGS: --check-alloc
// ERROR: line 25
trait Tr {
    type O;
}

struct Y;

impl Tr for Y {
    type O = &'static u64;
}

struct V<X: Tr> {
    o: X::O,
}

fn mk(gpa: Gpa) -> V<Y> {
    let b = Box::new_in(9u64, gpa);
    V { o: &*b }
}

fn main(gpa: Gpa) {
    let v = mk(gpa);
    println("{}", v.o);
}
